      answer: 2,
      marks: 1,
      explanation: "From s, only reading a 1 first reaches the final state p (a leading 0 sends the DFA into the dead trap state r). Once at p, a 0 self-loops (stays accepting), while a 1 moves to q, from which the only way back to an accepting state is another 1 (a 0 from q goes to the trap r). So after the initial 1, any interleaving of single 0's and 0-1 pairs \"11\" keeps the string accepted, giving 1(0+11)*."
